Additional source-reference imports, 5 October 2026:

QuestData also carries separately selected Classic/master, TBC and Retail
source editions. EntityData contains German/English item, spell and NPC names,
static tooltip prose and roles from MultiLanguage Classic/master. These are
source learning references, including seasonal records and historical values,
not verified current-client data. They never replace native quest observations
or game item/spell statistics. Attribution, author-permission basis reported by
the project owner, pinned revisions, raw source hashes, normalization and
exclusions are retained in QuestData/NOTICE and EntityData/NOTICE and their
source-manifest.json files. Original copyright remains with the respective
authors and Blizzard; no broader source licence is implied.

German word audio replacement, 13 October 2026:

The 122,049 OGG recordings under sounds/w were generated locally with
Fish Audio S2 Pro (https://huggingface.co/fishaudio/s2-pro), using the
project's approved synthetic female reference voice. The reference was
assembled from existing project Voxtral female quest narration; no voice
recording of a real person was used as the cloning reference.

Word recordings are distributed for noncommercial use under CC BY-NC 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
The Fish Audio model has its own Fish Audio Research License; a copy of
its supplied license is retained with the generation evidence under
verification/audio/fish-s2-pro-2026-10-13/. Model weights are not included.
The software's GPL license does not replace the audio or model terms.

The complete inventory and technical checks are retained in verification/audio.
Technical verification does not certify pronunciation: 51 clips carry review
flags. Historical Voxtral audit reports do not describe this replacement set.
